  "text": "Thanks so much for the question. This person is asking if they're betting $50 and winning at a high clip, will the retail books limit you? And the reality is it depends on a couple of things. So we all like to think we're smarter than we are, and I'm not saying you do or think this. I can lump myself in here. You know, the reality is how are you actually betting? So you're betting $50, okay, to be honest, the amount of money you're betting is irrelevant. It's how you're betting. Are you betting right before kickoff? Do you bet early in the week? Do you see closing line value? If you see closing line value, the answer is 100%. You're going to get limited. If you're betting right at kickoff, the reality is you may or may not get limited. Why? Because to be honest, you can't beat the closing line. You're not at the level, if you're betting $50, where you can beat the closing line. So to them, that is a signal that you're actually not a sharp bettor. You're just a lucky bettor. So it's just, it really depends on how you're betting, and I would say CLV is the quickest way you're going to get limited if you're betting early in the week.",
